-- title:
--   Cuspidal weight-two mod p forms killed by θ vanish
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $N \geq 1$ be an integer with $p \nmid N$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Inside the Laurent series field $K((q))$ write $\bar\jmath =$ `jqModC K` for the reduction of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNum` with coefficients pushed to $K$, and let `jqNModC K N` be its substitution $q \mapsto q^{N}$; the field `modularFunctionFieldC K N` is the intermediate field of $K((q))/K$ generated by these two elements. Let $G$ and $G_2$ be elements of that field. Assume `IsModPFormFn K 1 G`, that is: $G^{6}\,\bar\jmath^{4}(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{3}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra $K[\bar\jmath]$ of $K((q))$, and $G^{2}\,\bar\jmath\,(\bar\jmath - 1728)$ is integral over $K[\bar\jmath^{-1}]$. Writing $\theta = q\,d/dq$ and $\mathrm{qexp}(H) = H \cdot \theta\bar\jmath$ for the weight-one normalisation `qexpOfWeight K 1`, assume further that $G \cdot \theta\bar\jmath = (G_2 \cdot \theta\bar\jmath)^{p}$ in $K((q))$ and that the coefficient of $q^{0}$ in $G \cdot \theta\bar\jmath$ is zero. Then $G = 0$.
--
--   This is the geometric form, in terms of $q$-expansions lying in the level-$N$ modular function field in characteristic $p$, of Katz's theorem on the kernel of the operator $\theta$ acting on mod $p$ modular forms of weight two and level prime to $p$: a form whose $q$-expansion is a $p$-th power and which is cuspidal at infinity vanishes. It is used to derive the corresponding statement about power series, [`ModPForms.eq_zero_of_thetaPS_eq_zero_of_mem_modPCusp_two`](thm.html#ModPForms.eq_zero_of_thetaPS_eq_zero_of_mem_modPCusp_two).
